# Allow-list build context: only what the Dockerfile actually COPYs is sent to
# the daemon.  Everything else (docs, CI config, local .env / key / config
# files at any depth, editor clutter, build output) stays out of the build
# context, the builder layer cache and the provenance record.
#
# If the Dockerfile starts COPYing another path, add a `!` line for it here.

*

# Cargo workspace manifests + lockfile.
!Cargo.toml
!Cargo.lock

# All crate sources, but never a nested build directory or local secrets.
!crates
**/target
**/*.env
**/*.pem
**/*.key
**/*.crt
**/config.toml
!crates/**/Cargo.toml

# Entrypoint wrapper.
!docker
docker/*
!docker/entrypoint.sh
